---
id: convection-pork-chops
title: Convection-Baked Center-Cut Pork Chops
category: modular_protein

yield:
  servings: 2
  cooked_g: 320

storage:
  fridge_days: 4
  freezer_friendly: true

---

Pat @boneless-pork-center-chops{1%package} completely dry on all sides with paper towels.

Rub the chops evenly with @avocado-oil{1%tsp}, then coat all sides with @kosher-salt{1%tsp}, @black-pepper{0.5%tsp}, @garlic-powder{1%tsp}, @onion-powder{0.5%tsp}, and @dried-thyme{0.5%tsp}.

Set the #oven to convection 200°C (400°F) with an oven-safe #wire-rack inside a rimmed #sheet-pan. Arrange the chops on the rack with space between them and bake on the middle rack for ~bake-time{9%min} without flipping — the circulating air cooks both sides evenly.

Pull the moment the core temperature reaches 60°C (140°F) at the thickest part checked with a #meat-thermometer. Transfer to a warm plate, tent loosely with foil, and rest ~rest-time{4%min} — carryover brings the center to a juicy 63°C (145°F).

Divide into 2 meal prep containers (~160 g cooked each) and drizzle any rested juices over the portions.
